      "title": "Viatris Q3 Earnings Beat on Stronger Margins, Revenues Fall Y/Y",
      "summary": "Viatris (VTRS) beat Q3 adjusted EPS expectations at 71 cents versus 64 cents consensus, driven by margin expansion and strong Greater China sales growth of 14.2%. However, total revenues of $3.75 billion missed estimates and declined 0.3% year-over-year due to supply disruptions in Europe and Emerging Markets. The company raised full-year 2026 adjusted EPS guidance to $2.56-$2.63, though manufacturing suspension at its Nashik facility threatens Q4 revenues with an estimated $100 million impact.",
